          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For details see
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2"} Part 1-2 – Structured spectra
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_multiplicative_generalized_cohomology Relation to multiplicative generalized cohomology
          %p
            Under the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            represented by a ring spectrum inherits the structure of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
          %p
            Conversely via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} Brown representability theorem
            a spectrum representing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative cohomology theory
            inherits the structure of (at least) an H-ring spectrum. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "multiplicative+cohomology+theory#BrownRepresentabilityByRingSpectra"} there
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ultracommutative+ring+spectrum"} ultracommutative ring spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+ring+spectrum"} symmetric ring spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+algebra+spectrum"} symmetric algebra spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+spectrum"}> module spectrum
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+spectrum"} algebra spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gorenstein+ring+spectrum"} Gorenstein ring spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+with+smash+products"} functor with smash products
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/periodic+ring+spectrum"} periodic ring spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+ring+spectrum"} Hopf ring spectrum
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+ring+spectra"} model structure for ring spectra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"}> Boardman homomorphism
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+spectral+sequence"} multiplicative spectral sequence
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The notion of (commutative) homotopy ring spectra, i.e. (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"}> commutative
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            with respect to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
                , part III, section 10 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.uio.no/studier/emner/matnat/math/MAT9580/v17/documents/adams-shgh.pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (attributed there to
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Whitehead"} George Whitehead
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Michael+Boardman"}> John Michael Boardman
                , Sections 3,7 of:
                %em Stable Operations in Generalized Cohomology
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://math.jhu.edu/~wsw/papers2/math/28a-boardman-stable.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Boardman-StableOperations.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"} Ioan Mackenzie James
                (ed.)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
                Oxford 1995 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-444-81779-2.X5000-7"}> doi:10.1016/B978-0-444-81779-2.X5000-7
                )
            %li#BakerRichter04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Baker"}> Andrew Baker
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Birgit+Richter"} Birgit Richter
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Structured ring spectra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.cambridge.org/de/academic/subjects/mathematics/algebra/structured-ring-spectra?format=PB"} ISBN:9780521603058
            %li#TamakiKono06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"}> Dai Tamaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"} Akira Kono
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Cohomology
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeneralizedCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
            %li#Malkiewich14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cary+Malkiewich"}> Cary Malkiewich
                , section 1.3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The stable homotopy category
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.stanford.edu/~carym/stable.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory"} Introduction to Stable homotopy theory
                    –
                    %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+1-2#HomotopyRingSpectra"} Homotopy ring spectra
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Birgit+Richter"}> Birgit Richter
                ,
                %em Commutative ring spectra
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1710.02328"}> arXiv:1710.02328
                ,
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-hamburg.de/home/richter/rev-commringspectra.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+J.+Blumberg"} Andrew J. Blumberg
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Teena+Gerhardt"} Teena Gerhardt
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+A.+Hill"} Michael A. Hill
                (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+categories+and+structured+ring+spectra"} Stable categories and structured ring spectra
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H-infinity+ring+spectra"} H-infinity ring spectra
          %ul
            %li#BrunerMayMcLureSteinberger86
              R. Bruner,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+McClure"} James McClure
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi H
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_\infty
                  \-Ring Spectra and their Applications
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0075405"} doi:10.1007/BFb0075405
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/h_infty.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion of connective ring spectra as monoids with respect to a smash product on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gamma-spaces"} Gamma-spaces
          %ul
            %li#Schwede99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Stable homotopical algebra and
                    = succeed "-spaces" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Γ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/schwede/Gamma.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Lawson09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tyler+Lawson"}> Tyler Lawson
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Commutative Γ-rings do not model all commutative ring spectra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.hha/1296138517"} Euclid
          %p
            Discussion of ring spectra as rings with respect to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-modules"} S-modules
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Elmendorf"}> Anthony Elmendorf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"} Igor Kriz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Modern+foundations+for+stable+homotopy+theory"} Modern foundations for stable homotopy theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://hopf.math.purdue.edu/Elmendorf-Kriz-May/modern_foundations.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#EKMM
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anthony+Elmendorf"}> Anthony Elmendorf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Kriz"} Igor Kriz
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Mandell"} Michael Mandell
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} P. May
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rings%2C+modules+and+algebras+in+stable+homotopy+theory"} Rings, modules and algebras in stable homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/BOOKS/EKMM.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A comprehensive account for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Schwede12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Global+homotopy+theory"} Global homotopy theory
          %p
            An account in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            is in section 7.1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} simplicial
            ring spectra is in
          %ul
            %li#GoerssHopkins99
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              %em Simplicial Structured Ring Spectra
              (1999) (
              %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.34.9216"}> web
              )
          %p
            See also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
          %ul
            %li
              Glossary for stable and chromatic homotopy theory (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StableChromaticGlossary.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
